WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.069
In 1947, the mood in Taiwan gradually grew tense.

00:00:04.069 --> 00:00:08.106
A clash over contraband cigarettes sparked protests.

00:00:08.106 --> 00:00:11.508
People on the streets spoke quietly about the future.

00:00:11.508 --> 00:00:14.929
The government responded with force, causing many to suffer.

00:00:14.929 --> 00:00:19.100
Some died, some disappeared, and families were torn apart.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:23.083
At night in the city, lights went out one by one.

00:00:23.083 --> 00:00:26.114
Many families waited, but their loved ones never came home.

00:00:26.325 --> 00:00:30.675
This pain remained in people's hearts for a long time.

00:00:30.675 --> 00:00:34.910
For a long time, people dared not talk about it.

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:38.500
The truth was surrounded by silence and slowly forgotten.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:42.785
The younger generation began to ask about the stories of the past.

00:00:42.785 --> 00:00:45.835
Later, people began to commemorate the February 28 Incident.

00:00:45.835 --> 00:00:50.071
Every spring, fresh flowers are placed before the memorial.

00:00:50.071 --> 00:00:53.604
Candlelight sways quietly in the breeze.

00:00:53.604 --> 00:00:57.414
The incident became an issue of human rights and transitional justice.

00:00:57.414 --> 00:01:00.994
Remembering history is how we move toward a better future.
